# T4.2 case 4: a `password_cmd` that sleeps for thirty seconds.
#
# The connect thread is stuck in it, so what is being proved is that the loop
# is not: the help overlay opens and closes while the tab spins, `C` abandons
# the attempt, and `wait busy` comes back at once rather than in thirty
# seconds. The runner times the run to say which of the two it was.
key c
expect connecting

key ?
expect ╭ Help
expect Ctrl-T     next tab
frame help-while-connecting
key Esc
expect-not ╭ Help

key C
wait busy
expect ○
expect disconnected
frame abandoned

# An abandoned attempt animates nothing, however long it goes on sleeping.
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
wait 100
frame abandoned-idle
key q
